> > In "mi'e pier. mu'o" the object of "mu'o" is
> > any sumti, selbri, or bare name that comes after it; if there is none,
> it's
> > implicit "zo'e".
>
> Does an implicit "zo'e" really mean "anyone"?
>
> A: do mo
> B: gleki
>
> What word is implicit in the x1 of the second bridi, and what does it refer
> to?
>
>
> mu'o


There is no implicit x1. The x1 /is/ mi, because gleki is answering the
question {do mo}.

